From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:35:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: derive VHT160 NSS from radio chains

Use the radio TX NSS when applying the firmware bandwidth ratio,
then clamp the result to the peer NSS. Match the existing HE160
calculation and avoid reducing the receive NSS of a 2-stream peer
on a 4-chain radio reporting a 1:2 ratio.

Fixes: 18ab9d038fad ("wifi: ath12k: add support for 160 MHz bandwidth")
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261021165138.388593-3-julius@bairaktaris.de/
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/25807

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -2521,7 +2521,7 @@ static void ath12k_peer_assoc_h_vht(stru
 	arg->tx_max_mcs_nss = 0xFF;
 
 	if (arg->peer_phymode == MODE_11AC_VHT160) {
-		tx_nss = ath12k_get_nss_160mhz(ar, max_nss);
+		tx_nss = ath12k_get_nss_160mhz(ar, ar->num_tx_chains);
 		rx_nss = min(arg->peer_nss, tx_nss);
 		arg->peer_bw_rxnss_override = ATH12K_BW_NSS_MAP_ENABLE;
 
